WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.725
Each of these dangers is
ordinary, and each has a guard.

2
00:00:03.725 --> 00:00:07.607
The most tempting is sending a sample's
output straight to production,

3
00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:11.087
which lets pending workers and
duplicates into the directory.

4
00:00:11.087 --> 00:00:14.690
The most damaging is one bad
extract disabling hundreds

5
00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:18.063
of people before anyone looks,
and the hold stops that.

6
00:00:18.063 --> 00:00:21.488
The quietest is treating an
accepted response as success,

7
00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:24.200
when the record may have
failed inside the job.

8
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.914
Notice that every guard is something
the code does on every run,

9
00:00:27.914 --> 00:00:30.260
not something a person has to remember.
